From 6169e8e9616425ce93a49447af5df426f4325312 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett Heap <1513478+brettheap@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:41:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The code leg gets its own front door: the shape's leg
 AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and README.md, and the LF rule, ignore list and licence
 it lost when the root kept them.

Rehearsal patch for opensoft/openRepoTools#186, task T006 of
specs/004-migrate-to-triad/tasks.md, against run C's code leg 73b04d6. The
split left this leg with no AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md, LICENSE,
.gitattributes or .gitignore, because all six stayed in the assembly root,
and a superproject's attributes and ignore rules never reach into a
submodule's worktree.

- AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and README.md are openRepoShape 7f84ca4's
  templates/code-root/ files, rendered by its own copy_tree with this
  project's names, so the leg-clone detector in scripts/shape_advisory.py
  recognises them. Each AGENTS.md and README.md then adds one short section:
  where the suite runs, the pinned standard, where the manuals and the
  specifications now live, and where a feature's code and a bounded
  amendment are written.
- .gitattributes is the monorepo's own file, byte for byte (blob 3560973).
  Its reason, the installer's byte-for-byte comparisons, is this leg's.
  `git add --renormalize .` changes nothing here.
- .gitignore is the shape's templates/code-root/.gitignore, a superset of
  the three lines the monorepo ignored.
- LICENSE is the root's Apache-2.0 text, byte for byte (blob 261eeb9).

No executable, test or workflow is touched.

Lane: openRepoTools-1
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
